# g-issue-notifier

A serverless Telegram bot that monitors GitHub repositories for new issues and delivers instant notifications with a one-tap claim flow — built entirely on Cloudflare Workers, D1, Queues, and KV.

## How It Works
```
GitHub repo gets a new issue
          │
          ▼
Cron poller checks every N minutes (default: 10)
          │
          ▼
Cloudflare Queue fans out to dispatcher
          │
          ▼
Telegram notification with issue details + Claim button
          │
          ▼
Tap Claim → pick a template or write custom comment
          │
          ▼
Comment posted on GitHub as @yourghusername
```

## Features

- **Cron-based polling** — works on any public repo, no admin access needed
- **Label filters** — subscribe to specific labels per repo
- **Configurable poll interval** — set per subscription via Telegram
- **Claim flow** — one-tap comment on issues with saved templates or custom text
- **Native GitHub comments** — posts as your GitHub account via PAT, not a bot account
- **Multi-tenant ready** — schema and resolver support multiple users behind a feature flag
- **AES-GCM PAT encryption** — per-user PATs encrypted at rest when multi-tenant is enabled
- **Structured JSON logging** — trace IDs, log levels, consistent fields across all workers
- **TypeScript strict mode** — fully typed throughout

## Architecture
```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                      CLOUDFLARE EDGE                        │
│                                                             │
│   g-issue-notifier-bot          g-issue-notifier-poller     │
│   (Telegram webhook handler)    (Cron: */5 * * * *)         │
│                                                             │
│   g-issue-notifier-dispatcher                               │
│   (Queue consumer)                                          │
│                                                             │
│   D1: issuebot-db               Queue: issue-notifs         │
│   KV: SESSION, CLAIM_CTX                                    │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Workers

| Worker | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `g-issue-notifier-bot` | Handles all Telegram commands and callback queries |
| `g-issue-notifier-poller` | Cron job — polls GitHub API for new issues |
| `g-issue-notifier-dispatcher` | Queue consumer — formats and sends Telegram notifications |

### Storage

| Resource | Purpose |
|---|---|
| D1 `issuebot-db` | Subscriptions, label filters, templates, claims |
| KV `SESSION` | Conversation state for multi-step commands |
| KV `CLAIM_CTX` | Pending claim payloads (7 day TTL) |

## Telegram Commands

| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `/start` | Welcome message and command list |
| `/subscribe owner/repo` | Subscribe to a repository |
| `/unsubscribe` | Remove a subscription |
| `/subscriptions` | List active subscriptions and their label filters |
| `/newtemplate` | Create a new claim response template |
| `/templates` | View and delete saved templates |
| `/setinterval [mins]` | Set poll interval for a subscription (min: 5, default: 10) |
| `/help` | Show command list |

## Notification Format
```
New Issue  •  owner/repo

#42 — Issue title here

Description excerpt up to 300 chars...

──────────────────────────
Watching:    bug, help wanted
All Labels:  bug, help wanted, browser-compat
Reporter:    @janedoe
Maintainer:  Yes / No
Assignees:   None
Comments:    0
Opened:      2 minutes ago
──────────────────────────

[ Claim Issue ]   [ Open on GitHub ]
```

## Project Structure
```
g-issue-notifier/
├── src/
│   ├── workers/
│   │   ├── bot-handler.ts       # Telegram bot
│   │   ├── github-poller.ts     # Cron poller
│   │   ├── dispatcher.ts        # Queue consumer
│   │   ├── poller.toml          # Poller worker config
│   │   └── dispatcher.toml      # Dispatcher worker config
│   ├── lib/
│   │   ├── resolveUser.ts       # Single/multi-tenant user resolution
│   │   ├── github.ts            # GitHub API client
│   │   ├── telegram.ts          # Telegram API client
│   │   ├── crypto.ts            # AES-GCM PAT encryption
│   │   ├── logger.ts            # Structured JSON logger
│   │   └── utils.ts             # Shared utilities
│   └── types/
│       └── index.ts             # All shared TypeScript types
├── migrations/
│   ├── 0001_init.sql            # Initial schema
│   └── 0002_polling.sql         # Poll interval + last_checked_at
├── scripts/
│   ├── publish-secrets.ps1      # Push .dev.vars secrets to all workers
│   ├── publish-secrets.sh       # Bash equivalent
│   └── register-webhook.ps1     # Register Telegram webhook
├── .dev.vars                    # Local secrets (never committed)
├── .dev.vars.example            # Template for .dev.vars
└── wrangler.toml                # Bot handler worker config
```

## Setup

### Prerequisites

- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org) 18+
- [Wrangler CLI](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/wrangler/) — `npm install -g wrangler`
- [Cloudflare account](https://dash.cloudflare.com/sign-up)
- [Telegram bot token](https://t.me/BotFather) via @BotFather
- GitHub Personal Access Token with `repo` and `read:org` scopes

### 1. Clone and Install
```bash
git clone https://github.com/Malay-dev/g-issue-notifier.git
cd g-issue-notifier
npm install
```

### 2. Create Cloudflare Resources
```bash
wrangler login

wrangler d1 create issuebot-db
wrangler kv namespace create SESSION
wrangler kv namespace create CLAIM_CTX
wrangler queues create issue-notifs
```

Copy the IDs from each command output into `wrangler.toml`, `src/workers/poller.toml`, and `src/workers/dispatcher.toml`.

### 3. Run Migrations
```bash
npm run db:migrate:remote
```

### 4. Configure Secrets

Copy `.dev.vars.example` to `.dev.vars` and fill in all values:
```bash
cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
```
```ini
BOT_TOKEN=your_telegram_bot_token
GH_PAT=your_github_personal_access_token
WEBHOOK_SECRET=random_secret_string
ENCRYPTION_KEY=64_char_hex_string
OWNER_CHAT_ID=your_telegram_chat_id
OWNER_GH_USER=your_github_username
OWNER_ID=any_uuid_v4
MULTI_TENANT=false
LOG_LEVEL=info
```

Generate `ENCRYPTION_KEY`:
```bash
node -e "const b = new Uint8Array(32); crypto.getRandomValues(b); console.log(Array.from(b).map(x => x.toString(16).padStart(2,'0')).join(''))"
```

Get your `OWNER_CHAT_ID` by messaging [@userinfobot](https://t.me/userinfobot) on Telegram.

Push secrets to all workers:
```bash
npm run secrets:publish
```

### 5. Deploy
```bash
npm run deploy:all
```

### 6. Register Telegram Webhook
```bash
npm run webhook:register
```

## Available Scripts

| Script | Description |
|---|---|
| `npm run deploy:all` | Deploy all three workers |
| `npm run deploy:bot` | Deploy bot handler only |
| `npm run deploy:poller` | Deploy poller only |
| `npm run deploy:dispatcher` | Deploy dispatcher only |
| `npm run tail:bot` | Live logs for bot handler |
| `npm run tail:poller` | Live logs for poller |
| `npm run tail:dispatcher` | Live logs for dispatcher |
| `npm run db:migrate:remote` | Apply migrations to remote D1 |
| `npm run db:migrate:local` | Apply migrations to local D1 |
| `npm run secrets:publish` | Push .dev.vars secrets to all workers |
| `npm run webhook:register` | Register Telegram webhook |
| `npm run typecheck` | Run TypeScript type checking |

## Secrets Reference

| Secret | Workers | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `BOT_TOKEN` | bot, dispatcher | Telegram bot token from @BotFather |
| `GH_PAT` | bot, poller, dispatcher | GitHub Personal Access Token |
| `WEBHOOK_SECRET` | bot, poller, dispatcher | Random string for request validation |
| `ENCRYPTION_KEY` | bot, poller, dispatcher | 32-byte hex key for AES-GCM PAT encryption |
| `OWNER_CHAT_ID` | bot, poller, dispatcher | Your Telegram chat ID |
| `OWNER_GH_USER` | bot, poller, dispatcher | Your GitHub username |
| `OWNER_ID` | bot, poller, dispatcher | Stable UUID used as your user_id in D1 |

## Multi-Tenant Mode

The system is designed for single-user mode by default but is schema-ready for multiple users.

To enable multi-tenant mode, flip the flag in all three worker toml files:
```toml
[vars]
MULTI_TENANT = "true"
```

In multi-tenant mode:
- Users are registered in the `users` table on `/start`
- Each user's PAT is encrypted with AES-GCM before storage in D1
- The `ENCRYPTION_KEY` secret is the only key that can decrypt PATs

## Secret Rotation

| Secret | How to rotate |
|---|---|
| `BOT_TOKEN` | @BotFather → `/mybots` → your bot → Revoke token → re-run `secrets:publish` + `webhook:register` |
| `GH_PAT` | GitHub → Settings → Tokens → delete old → generate new → re-run `secrets:publish` |
| `WEBHOOK_SECRET` | Generate new hex string → re-run `secrets:publish` |
| `ENCRYPTION_KEY` | Generate new key → re-encrypt all PATs in D1 → re-run `secrets:publish` |

